@startuml

title ores.marketdata.client Component

set namespaceSeparator ::

namespace ores #F2F2F2 {
    namespace marketdata #F2F2F2 {
        namespace client #F2F2F2 {
            class market_data_client {
                -nats_ : ores::nats::service::nats_client&
                +market_data_client(ores::nats::service::nats_client& nats)
                +save_series(const vector<domain::market_series>& series) : [[nodiscard]] expected<int, string>
                +save_observations(const vector<domain::market_observation>& observations) : [[nodiscard]] expected<int, string>
                +list_observations(const string& series_id) : [[nodiscard]] expected<vector<domain::market_observation>, string>
                +list_observations_page(const string& series_id, uint32_t offset, uint32_t limit) : [[nodiscard]] expected<vector<domain::market_observation>, string>
                +list_feed_bindings() : [[nodiscard]] expected<vector<domain::feed_binding>, string>
                +save_feed_binding(const domain::feed_binding& binding) : [[nodiscard]] expected<bool, string>
            }
        }
    }
}

' --- manual: everything below this line is hand-authored; the script preserves it ---

' Relationships the automated pass cannot see.
'
' The generator emits a box per class with its members and no edges, so every
' line below is read from the code rather than derived from it. A data member
' is ownership (*--); a type that appears only in a signature is a dependency
' (..>). Types from another component are left out, per the class-diagram
' conventions.

' No component-local edges: this part names only its own types and types from other components.

' The parser drops a declaration whose parameter default carries braces. Both
' public methods below have one, so the generated box omits them.

class ores::marketdata::client::market_data_client {
    +list_series(series_type : const string&) : [[nodiscard]] expected<vector<domain::market_series>, string>
    +find_series_by_uri(oresmd_uri : const string&, party_id : const string&) : [[nodiscard]] expected<optional<domain::market_series>, string>
}
note right of "ores::marketdata::client::market_data_client"
Every call goes through the authenticated nats_client that the
constructor stores by reference, so that client must outlive this
object. Each method returns std::expected: the decoded response, or
an error string on transport, authorisation, or decode failure.
list_series() accepts series_type and ignores it, because the
canonical list request carries no series-type filter.
find_series_by_uri() reads one generous page (limit 10000) and matches
the identity client-side; with no party_id the first id-ordered match
wins.
end note

